  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 4-Heptanone and Neuropilin-2, mediated through Phosphodiesterase 6C. This pathway is supported by multiple independent connections, with 4-Heptanone directly targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C, which in turn is targeted by Adenaflorine C and another compound, (1S,6S,14R,18S)-6,10,10,14,15,21,21-heptamethyl-3,24-dioxaheptacyclo[16.5.2.01,15.02,4.05,14.06,11.018,23]pentacosane-9,25-dione. These compounds all ultimately target Neuropilin-2, indicating a possible mechanism of action involving the inhibition of a phosphodiesterase enzyme, which may modulate signaling pathways related to Neuropilin-2 function. The consistent presence of Phosphodiesterase 6C as a common target across these compounds supports a plausible biological role in the interaction between 4-Heptanone and Neuropilin-2. The evidence is robust, but further investigation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the functional significance of this interaction in the context of Neuropilin-2 activity.",
